== Baking Leveling Guide (Detailed) ==

[[File:BakingDuxa.png|right|frame|An oven in Freeport]]
[[File:Npc katha firespinner.png|alt=Katha Firespinner|thumb|380x380px|Batwing Merchant in EC]]
You need about 10pp and an hour of your time to get to skill 135 (assuming you sell back what you make). Skill ups after that become more time consuming and costly. Evil races, including Iksars, can take advantage of the [[Rohand's Brandy]] quest in Qeynos in order to raise faction with Freeport merchants.
NB : get your Int or Wis to a decent level, for this not being a hell to upgrade. you can go from 1 hour only to 4 hour clicking to get it upgraded if you have like no more than 60 int.

''Ingredients for 1-135:''
* [[Bat Wing]]
* [[Frosting]]
* [[Fresh Fish]]
* [[Jug of Sauces]]


Note on "stacks": When reading below you will be instructed to buy stacks of items. Keep in mind this guide was written when the maximum stack of an item was 20. On EQL most trade skill items can stack to 1000. So when the guide says "buy 10 stacks of <item>" what they mean is buy 200 of that item.

Note on skills on EQL: Skills on EQL occur much more often than other versions of Everquest. Keep that in mind when collecting/buying items. You will likely need far less that this guide suggests!
=== Step 1: [[Batwing Crunchies]] ===

If '''Good:'''

* Go to [[West Freeport]]
* [[Lysa Truegreen]] (2nd floor of caster guild): buy 10 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s (Make sure you read the note just above about stacks!)
* [[Pincia Brownloe]] (Building across from monk guild): buy 10 stacks of [[frosting]]

'''''Note:''' [[Pincia Brownloe]] appears to be willing to sell to anyone. (Every character I've tried so far anyway, including an iksar necromancer.)
''

If '''Evil:'''

* Go to [[East Commonlands]]
* [[Katha Firespinner]] (Inn near WC zoneline - She doesn't sell to Trolls.): buy 10 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s - 3/2022 Would not sell to Rallos Zek Ogre Shaman with dubious faction.
* Go to [[Neriak|Neriak Commons]]
* [[Niz L`Crit]] (refined palate, next to bank): buy 10 stacks of [[frosting]] - 3/2022 Beware of [[Razran F`Lok]]. He paths at the Neriak Down Under entrance to bank area.

If '''Iksar:'''

* Go to [[Field of Bone]]
* [[Klok Acet]] (near entrance to Cabilis): buy 10 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s
* Go to [[East Cabilis]]
* [[Klok Sweetzie]] (near bank): buy 10 stacks of [[Frosting]]

THEN:

* Go to your favorite oven (or use a [[spit]] if you want to lug one around)
* Make [[Batwing Crunchies]] till skill '''46''': 1 [[Bat Wing]], 1 [[Frosting]].
* Sell leftover [[Frosting]] and [[Batwing Crunchies]].
* '''KEEP extra [[Bat Wing]]s'''

=== Step 2: [[Fish Fillets]] ===

If '''Good:'''

* Go to [[East Freeport]]
* [[Tanlok Harson]] (port authority at dock, second floor): buy 10 stacks of [[Fresh Fish]]
* [[Sun Alemaker]] (Trader's Holiday - the oven is right behind her) : buy 10 stacks of [[Jug of Sauces]]

If '''Evil:'''

* Go to [[Neriak|Neriak Commons]]
* [[Niz L'Crit]] (refined palate, next to bank): buy 10 stacks of [[Jug of Sauces]]
* [[Mariz Ixtaz]] (near Toadstool): buy 30 stacks of [[Fresh Fish]]

If '''Iksar'''

* Go to [[Cabilis|East Cabilis]]
* [[Klok Sweetzie]] (near bank): buy 10 stacks of [[Jug of Sauces]]
* Check all vendors, and try to buy as much [[Fresh Fish]] as you can find.
* Then grab a pole and hit the fishing button till you have 30 stacks. (I told you to go to Freeport)

'''''Note:''' Iksar necromancers level 34+ with [[Call of Bones]] (skeleton illusion) can buy [[Fresh Fish]] from the merchants inside the Port Authority
''

THEN:

* Go to your favorite oven (or use a spit if you want to lug one around)
* Make [[Fish Fillets]] till skill '''82''': 1 [[Fresh Fish]], 1 [[Jug of Sauces]]
* Sell extra [[Jug of Sauces|Jugs of Sauces]] and [[Fish Fillets]].
* '''KEEP extra [[Fresh Fish]]'''

=== Step 3: [[Fish Rolls]] ===

If '''Good:'''

* Go to [[West Freeport]]
* [[Lysa Truegreen]] (2nd floor of caster guild): buy 20 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s 
* Go to [[East Freeport]]
* [[Tanlok Harson]] (port authority at dock): buy 20 stacks of [[Fresh Fish]] (including leftovers from step 2)

If '''Evil:'''

* Go to [[East Commonlands]]
* [[Katha Firespinner]] (Inn near [[West Commonlands]] zoneline): buy 20 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s (including leftovers from step 1)
* Go to [[Neriak|Neriak Commons]]
* [[Mariz Ixtaz]] (near Toadstool): buy 20 stacks of [[Fresh Fish]] (including leftovers from step 2)

If '''Iksar:'''

* Go to [[Field of Bone]]
* [[Klok Acet]] (near entrance to [[Cabilis|East Cabilis]]): buy 20 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s (including leftovers from step 1)
* Check all vendors, and try to buy as much [[Fresh Fish]] as you can find.
* Then grab a pole and hit the fishing button till you have 20 stacks of [[Fresh Fish]] (including leftovers from step 2). (I told you to go to Freeport)

THEN:

* Go to your favorite [[oven]] (or use a [[spit]] if you want to lug one around)
* Make [[Fish Rolls]] till skill '''135''': 1 [[Bat Wing]], 1 [[Fresh Fish]]
* Sell all leftover [[Fresh Fish]]
* '''KEEP extra [[Bat Wing]]s'''
* Use [[Fish Rolls]] (these are very popular items, especially among monks)

=== Step 4: [[Batwing Pie]] ===

This is where it starts to become more expensive and time consuming. ''Note: On p1999 you can/may need to use Snake Eggs to make clumps of dough until 142.''

'''Good/Evil''': 

''(It should be noted that [[Clump of Dough|Clumps of Dough]] can be created from different kinds of eggs, which yield different quantities of dough. Basilisk eggs (farmed in [[Lavastorm Mountains]]) have a great drop rate and provide 15 [[Clump of Dough|Clumps of Dough]] per successful combine.)''
* Go to [[Lavastorm Mountains]]
* Kill [[A Lava Basilisk|Lava Basilisk]]s till you get 15 [[Basilisk Egg]]s
* Acquire a [[Pie Tin]] (see smithing or pottery recipes for more info. Personally, I recommend pottery. It is far easier and cheaper).

If '''Good:'''
* Go to [[West Freeport]]
* [[Pincia Brownloe]] (unlabeled building next to monk's guild, W Freeport): buy a [[Mixing Bowl]], 15 [[Bottle of Milk|Bottles of Milk]], 15 [[Cup of Flour|Cups of Flour]], and 10 stacks of [[Spices]].
* [[Lysa Truegreen]] (2nd level of caster building): buy 10 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s (including leftovers from step 3)
* Remember these 2 merchants, if/when you run out of stacks just return and stock again.

If '''Evil:'''

* Go to Neriak Foreign Quarter
* [[Sal Drana]] (human side): buy a [[Mixing Bowl]]
* Go to [[Neriak|Neriak Commons]]
* [[Niz L`Crit]] (refined palate, next to bank): buy 15 [[Bottle of Milk|Bottles of Milk]], 15 [[Cup of Flour|Cups of Flour]], and 10 stacks of [[Spices]]
* Go to [[East Commonlands]]
* [[Katha Firespinner]] (inn 3): buy 10 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s (including leftovers from step 3)

If '''Iksar:'''

''It is much easier if you go to [[Freeport]], but if you insist on staying in [[Kunark]]...''
* Go to [[The Overthere]]
* Hunt [[A stonegazer cockatrice|Stonegazer Cockatrice]] or [[Forage]] till you get 45 [[Cockatrice Egg]]s 

''3 times as many eggs are needed as the '''Good/Evil''' routes because [[Cockatrice Egg]]s only yield 5 [[Clump of Dough|Clumps of Dough]] per successful combine, whereas [[Basilisk Egg]]s yield 15''
* Go to [[Field of Bone]]
* [[Klok Acet]] (near entrance to [[Cabilis|East Cabilis]]): buy 10 stacks of [[Bat Wing]]s (including leftovers from step 3)
* Go to [[Cabilis|East Cabilis]]
* [[Klok Sweetzie]] (near bank): buy 45 [[Bottle of Milk|Bottles of Milk]], 45 [[Cup of Flour|Cups of Flour]], and 10 stacks of [[Spices]]

THEN:

* Make [[Clump of Dough|Clumps of Dough]] in [[Mixing Bowl]]. They are long since trivial for you: 1 [[Basilisk Egg]], 1 [[Cup of Flour]], 1 [[Bottle of Milk]] (yields 15 [[Clump of Dough|Clumps of Dough]])
* Make [[Batwing Pie]] (in [[Oven]]) until skill '''142''': 1 [[Bat Wing]], 1 [[Clump of Dough]], 1 [[Spices]], 1 [[Pie Tin]] (you get the tin back).
* All this can be done in [[West Freeport]]. An [[Oven]] is located in an unnamed building behind the monk guild, over the bridge.
* Sell extra [[Bat Wing]]s and [[Batwing Pie]]s.
* '''KEEP extra [[Clump of Dough|Clumps of Dough]]'''.

=== Step 5: Cakes ===

All people:

* Go to Greater or Lesser Faydark
* Hunt Brownies for their parts.
* Make White Chocolate: 2 frosting, 1 spices, 1 brownie parts (in a mixing bowl)
* And/or Make Winter Chocolate: 2 frosting, 1 brownie parts (in a mixing bowl)

THEN:

* Make Wedding  cakes till '''162''': 1 White Chocolate, 1 Frosting, 1 Clump of Dough  
* OR -- Make Birthday cakes till '''162''': 1 Winter Chocolate, 1 Frosting, 1 Clump of Dough
* Both require a Cake Round (Smithing or Pottery) which you get back after combine

=== Step 6: Pixie Powdered Cinnesticks ===

All people:

* Go to Greater or Lesser Faydark
* Buy or Forage [[Cinnamon Sticks]]
* Hunt Pixies for Pixie dust
* Make Pixie Powder Cinnesticks till trivial '''(>200)''': 3 Pixie Dust, 1 Cinnamon Stick (in a mixing bowl)

'''NOTE: [[A pixie jongleur]] gives you negative faction hits to: Guards of Qeynos (-30), Jaggedpine Treefolk (-30), Protectors of Pine (-30). QRG Protected Animals (-30).  Kill with a character that doesn't care about those faction hits or find a way to kill these pixies without getting a faction hit if this is a concern with you.  You will have to kill hundreds, maybe thousands to get enough pixie dusts to get to 202 skill! '''

=== Step 7: Dragon Steaks ===

All people:

* Get Dragon meat however you can (it is a rare drop off Velious dragons), and make Dragon Steaks till trivial.

Then come back and tell us what the trivial is: 1 Dragon Meat, 1 Jug of Sauces, 1 Spices.

